
  [1mThe choice:[0m do the filters stay visible above the table, or sit behind a button?

  - [1mA. Inline filter bar.[0m All nine types and the dates are visible, so finding "Sign-in failed" takes one click. Least
    JS and markup, which helps with the 300-line limit and a strict review. It takes up vertical space above the table
    and stacks into a column on narrow screens. Switching to B later is fairly cheap because the controls are the same.
  - [1mB. "Filters" button with a popover and tags.[0m Compact, and the tags show which filters are active. It needs an extra
    click plus popover focus, Escape and outside-click handling, so there's more code and more for accessibility review
    to check (VoiceOver and NVDA).

  [1mMy recommendation is A.[0m The complaint is that people can't find things, and hiding the filters behind a button works
  against that. A also keeps the diff smaller.

  Tell me which one here in the terminal. Clicking an option in the tab works too.

